{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3371","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3371","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3371\",\"parent_revision\":\"b75bb2180b521b7063db05c706972caff64397d98a6aa1fe07c91b846da03dad\",\"root_revision\":\"b75bb2180b521b7063db05c706972caff64397d98a6aa1fe07c91b846da03dad\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-01\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nA four-angle automated code review of PR #3366 (#2287 slice B: collapse capability-gap dialects B/C/H) surfaced four reuse/simplification/altitude findings. All four are about code introduced by #2287 slice 1 (#3360, \\\"gate GitHubExtras on a capability flag\\\") already merged to main before slice B's branch existed \u2014 confirmed by diffing PR #3366 against its merge-base, which touches none of the files below. Not actioned in #3366; filed here for a dedicated follow-up PR after #3366 merges.\\n\\n1. **`_capability_gates.py:224-251` vs `:254-275`** \u2014 `require_github_extras` and `require_branch_support` are a 1:1 copy-paste (flag-getattr check \u2192 raise, isinstance check \u2192 raise-with-protocol_mismatch, return backend), differing only in the capability-name string and Protocol type. The module's own docstring signals intent to add more gated capabilities later, which today means copy-pasting a third near-identical ~12-line function rather than extending one generic helper.\\n\\n2. **`sync_engine.py:92-103`** (`_count(result, key)`) re-implements the same \\\"read dict field, default 0, drop if not int\\\" narrowing already in `operations.py:2541-2555` (`_int_field`). Same logic maintained in two places; a future dict-shape change (e.g. treating `None` as a valid \\\"unknown\\\" sentinel) has to be fixed in both or they silently diverge.\\n\\n3. **`tests/test_github_extras_capability_gate.py:29-41`** (`sqlite_backend` fixture) and **`tests_backlog/test_backlog_backend_capability_contract.py:211-220`** (`_close_if_sqlite()`) independently work around the same SQLiteBackend leaked-connection `ResourceWarning` (AGENTS.md strict-warnings policy), both added by slice 1. A third test file needing a SQLiteBackend will likely add a third copy instead of pulling a shared conftest fixture.\\n\\n4. **`server.py`** at `list_issues` (~4747), `comment_issue` (~4788), `list_comments` (~4831), `read_comment` (~4908) \u2014 the fix for a generic `except (GithubException, BacklogError)` handler swallowing/re-wrapping `UnsupportedBackendCapabilityError` (discarding its structured fields) was applied as `except UnsupportedBackendCapabilityError: raise` pasted identically ahead of the existing handler at each of the 4 call sites, rather than as one shared wrapper around the GitHub-error-translation boilerplate all 4 functions already share. This is exactly the class of per-call-site patch #2287 itself was meant to eliminate \u2014 a 5th GitHub-calling function added later will silently re-wrap the typed error unless someone remembers to paste the guard again.\\n\\nUser-provided context: no fix has been designed yet for any of these \u2014 design the actual approach (e.g. a single generic `_require_capability` helper for #1, reusing `_int_field` for #2, a shared conftest fixture for #3, and a decorator or context manager around the GitHub-error-translation boilerplate for #4) during grooming, not here.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Multi-angle code review of PR #3366 (four parallel finder agents, /code-review high --fix)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-01\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"093f016ec8954786df666295c57e89424f77e17cf4d4734b83416152a731ab5f\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABR0i-Vg\"}"}